(Cell Division and Study Guide) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cells reproduce by dividing. In mitosis, a eukaryotic cell divides to produce two) Tj
T*
(genetically identical daughter cells. Mitosis is used for growth, repair, and asexual) Tj
T*
(reproduction. The cell cycle includes interphase, mitosis, and cytokinesis. Interphase is) Tj
T*
(divided into G1, S, and G2 phases. DNA is replicated during the S phase.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Meiosis produces gametes with half the normal number of chromosomes. It involves two rounds) Tj
T*
(of division and creates genetic variation through crossing over and independent assortment.) Tj
T*
(Fertilization restores the diploid chromosome number.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Key facts to remember:) Tj
T*
(1. The plasma membrane is a phospholipid bilayer that controls what enters and leaves the) Tj
T*
(cell.) Tj
T*
(2. Mitochondria produce most of the cell's ATP through aerobic respiration.) Tj
T*
(3. Ribosomes translate mRNA into proteins.) Tj
T*
(4. The nucleus contains DNA and controls gene expression.) Tj
T*
(5. ATP is the universal energy currency of the cell.) Tj
T*
(6. Enzymes are biological catalysts that lower activation energy.) Tj
T*
(7. Prokaryotic cells lack a membrane-bound nucleus; eukaryotic cells have one.) Tj
T*
(8. Active transport requires ATP, while passive transport does not.) Tj
T*
(9. The electron transport chain produces the largest amount of ATP in aerobic respiration.) Tj
T*
(10. Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Review questions:) Tj
T*
(- What is the main function of the plasma membrane?) Tj
T*
(- Which organelle produces most of the ATP in a eukaryotic cell?) Tj
T*
(- What are the inputs and outputs of aerobic respiration?) Tj
T*
(- How do prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells differ?) Tj
T*
(- Where does translation take place?) Tj
T*
